{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"loss function loss function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md","fileName":"Loss Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Loss Function","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Optimization and Differentiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Squared Error Loss","Categorical Cross-Entropy","Gradient Descent","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"loss function loss function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md","fileName":"Loss Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Loss Function","heading":"Loss Function","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A loss function measures the difference between a machine-learning model's actual output and the desired output. It turns error into a numerical objective that training can minimize.\n\nDifferent outputs require different measures. [[Squared Error Loss]] can compare individual values, while [[Categorical Cross-Entropy]] compares a predicted probability distribution with a target distribution. Backpropagation uses derivatives of the loss to guide parameter updates.\n\nKelleher uses a sum of squared errors to score how a candidate linear function fits labeled examples. Squaring prevents errors above and below their targets from canceling, and minimizing that score supplies a concrete objective for [[Gradient Descent]]. The score is also a fitness measure for comparing candidate functions; choosing the measure is part of the learning problem, not a neutral detail after the model has been built.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Squared Error Loss","Categorical Cross-Entropy","Gradient Descent","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"loss function loss function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Loss Function.md","fileName":"Loss Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Loss Function","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Squared Error Loss","Categorical Cross-Entropy","Gradient Descent","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}